<title>DENMARK: DANISH CODAN SIX-MONTH 1997 PROFIT RISES.</title>
<headline>DANISH CODAN SIX-MONTH 1997 PROFIT RISES.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>					  (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Group pre-tax result		  511 vs 441</p>
<p> Net result after minorities	494  vs  555</p>
<p> Gross premiums, accident	  1,820 vs  1,822</p>
<p> Gross premiums, life		  736 vs  696</p>
<p> Balance end-June 1997	    59,485 vs  53,669 end-June 1996</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Denmark's second biggest insurer is A/S Forsikringsselskabet Codan. It is 71.45 percent owned by Britain's Royal &amp; Sun Alliance. It said in a statement that it upheld its earlier expectations of similar insurance results in 1997's second half to 1996.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33-969652</p>
</text>
